    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618-a2">

                <pb facs="1134" n="1010" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1010"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    94.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Giers to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 3 (15),
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: His Majesty the Emperor, deeply
                    touched by the sentiments which you express on behalf of the President and
                    people of the United States, as well as in your own name, on the occasion of the
                    grievous loss which has stricken Russia, charges me to thank you for these
                    testimonials of sympathy.</p>
                <p>Receive, Mr. Minister, the assurance of my most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>GIERS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
